# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Context Map

## Read route

`AGENTS.md` → this map → task manifest when applicable → lightweight indexes → selected canonical frontmatter → selected bodies.

## Tree

| Path | Role | Authority |
|---|---|---|
| `PROJECT.md` | Project identity and durable overview | Canonical |
| `docs/architecture.md` | System boundaries and invariants | Canonical |
| `docs/features/*/overview.md` | Feature context and ownership | Canonical |
| `docs/features/*/contracts.md` | Boundary contracts | Canonical |
| `docs/requirements/*.md` | Atomic accepted requirements | Canonical |
| `work/items/*.md` | One objective, lifecycle, order, optional tasks and outcome | Canonical |
| `docs/decisions/*.md` | Durable decisions | Canonical |
| `sources/records/*.md` | Import provenance and dispositions | Canonical |
| `docs/*/INDEX.md`, `work/INDEX.md`, `sources/INDEX.md` | Selection views derived from canonical metadata | Generated |
| `tasks/*` | Active transient execution state | Transient until promoted |
| `tasks/*/TASK_STATE.md` | Stable task UUID, owner, revision, source binding and next action | Canonical active handoff |
| `tasks/*/chats/*/MEMORY.md` | Separate notes and association for each chat binding | Canonical active memory |
| `docs/reports/closures/*.md` | Concise durable closure conclusions | Canonical |
| `.local/archives/*` | Raw closed task and chat memory | Local archive |
| `.local/chat-index.json` | Reverse lookup projected from chat records | Generated, local |
| `.local/state.json` | Resolver and schema state only | Machine-readable, local |
| `.local/context-operations/*.json` | Recoverable work item writes | Local journal |

## Context levels

- `none`: do not load.
- `contract`: load only the feature boundary contract and selected requirements.
- `feature`: load the feature definition plus relevant contracts and requirements.
- `deep`: add decisions and reports associated with the selected feature, without loading unrelated history.

Dependencies do not recursively inherit context levels.

## Loss prevention

Indexes can be deleted and rebuilt from canonical files. Closure must classify and promote durable task discoveries before finalization. If classification is uncertain, preserve the information as a proposed work item or unresolved closure finding.

Memory need not own a checkout. Source modes are none, read-only, isolated, and existing. Only a clean, explicitly Deep Context-owned worktree is eligible for cleanup; borrowed checkouts and source branches are retained. Shared task changes require the owner binding and expected state revision. Interrupted writes are reported for explicit repair-tasks; read-only resolution never repairs or guesses.

One work item owns each objective. Accepted statuses are proposed, planned, active, blocked, done and merged. Optional integer order applies to proposed/planned work. Plans, checkpoints and handoffs belong in tasks/; preserve historical hashes and raw journals in .local/. Work completion and task closure are independent.
